cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (this file) and the paper listed under preferred-citation."
title: "Localizable bottom-up apartment household load model"
abstract: >-
  A localizable, decomposable bottom-up model of residential electricity
  demand in apartment dwellings (without electric space heating, electric
  domestic hot water or electric-vehicle charging), with resolution down
  to one second. Probabilistic occupancy (a Markov chain driven by a
  time-use survey) switches appliances with measured power traces, and
  the seasonal shape is localized by the national standard load profile,
  so no local time-use survey is required. Demand can be decomposed down
  to the individual appliance, which enables efficiency scenarios.
  Reactive power is computed bottom-up as the sum of each appliance's
  active-power profile scaled by its measured displacement power factor
  (values from Hannagan et al. 2023), with an optional per-connection-point
  capacitive offset for non-appliance contributions such as LV cabling.
  Includes a PySide6 desktop application and an optional pvlib/PVGIS
  photovoltaic chain.
type: software
